  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Equality in Action Volunteer Cooperation Program for Partner Development inGhana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a seven (7 -year) collaboration between Ghana and Oxfam Quebec and will be implemented through two main mechanisms, namely volunteer training and technical support for partner growth and local grants for partners to address societal issues affecting most vulnerable groups including women and girls. Six (6) partners: Widows and Orphans Movement (WOM), Youth Empowerment for Life (YEFL), Women in Law and Development in Africa (WILDAF), Foundation for Security and Development in Africa (FOSDA), Northern Sector Action Awareness Centre (NORSAAC), Centre for Public Interest Law (CEPIL) will benefit from the program initially. The level of impact will be in Ghana.</narrative>
  </description>
